{"t": 1794117242.661834, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": ":rotating_light: checkout \u2014 PaymentGatewayErrors (AG-7731, critical)\n\nWhat: Gateway 4xx rate ~38% on checkout since 07:41 UTC. Every charge attempt is being rejected.\n\nCause: the payment gateway switched to API version 2026-11 (\"strict amounts\"). It now requires `amount` as an integer in minor units (cents); checkout was still sending a decimal euro amount.\nLog evidence: `WARN gateway rejected charge status=400 body={\"error\":\"invalid_amount\",\"message\":\"amount must be an integer in minor units (cents), got 12.34\"}` followed by `INFO gateway api version switched to 2026-11 (strict amounts)`.\n\nFix: `checkout/gateway.py` \u2014 `charge_payload()` now converts EUR to integer cents with Decimal half-up rounding (12.34 -> {\"amount\": 1234, \"currency\": \"EUR\"}). Verified locally across representative amounts; no other payload fields change.\n\nNext: deploy checkout and watch gateway 4xx rate back to baseline; confirm charges succeed end-to-end."}, "ok": true}
